      "side": 1,
      "message": "For reference, the truncation warning is defined directly in AOSP Bionic:\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/bionic/+/refs/heads/main/libc/system_properties/system_properties.cpp\n\n\"media.stagefright.thumbnail.prefer_hw_codecs\" is 44 characters long, exceeding PROP_NAME_MAX (32). \n\nWhen calling legacy property_get_bool(), Bionic\u0027s SystemProperties::Read() truncates the name and logs the error via async_safe_format_log. Because it writes directly to Android\u0027s logd rather than stdout/stderr, a standalone C test executable won\u0027t output anything to the console, but it triggers immediately in logcat on-device:\n\"E libc: The property name length for \u0027media.stagefright.thumbnail.prefer_hw_codecs\u0027 is \u003e\u003d 31...\"\n\nMigrating to android::base::GetBoolProperty() uses __system_property_read_callback, avoiding legacy property name limits.",
